{"id":"fast-and-connected","title":"Are the consistently fast ones connected?","question":"Do the firms that are consistently fast give to campaigns, lobby, give gifts, register as permit consultants, hold City contracts, or appear in a case file?","finding":"Of 105 named firms that are consistently fast on any measure, 44 have at least one recorded connection and 61 have none. 36 have staff or owners who gave to candidates for City office since 2012 ($135,242 in all), 7 are clients of registered lobbyists, 3 gave a gift to a City official or department, 4 are on the Ethics Commission's permit-consultant register, 16 were paid $100,000 or more by the City since fiscal 2019, 0 employ a person matched by name to former City staff, and 1 is named in a case file or on Building Inspection's extra-scrutiny list. Each of these connections is an exact name match.","how":"For every named firm that meets a test in the screens above (speed, counter path, holds and stations, or another permit system): contributions to candidates' own committees since 2012 where the donor lists the firm as employer, or the firm itself gave; contacts with City officials reported by registered lobbyists naming the firm as client; gifts to officials (Form 700) and to departments, and gifts of travel; the Ethics Commission's permit-consultant register; City payments since fiscal 2019 of $100,000 or more; former City staff now at a firm, from this project's name-matched list of former staff (the site’s “People and roles” page); and the firms and people named in the building-inspection and Public Works case files and on Building Inspection's extra-scrutiny list. Firms are matched on the exact normalised name. A licensed individual is matched to a donor only when the donor's stated employer or occupation also fits.","limits":"Large firms do all of them whether or not they are fast. A name match can be wrong: two firms can share a name, and an employer typed on a campaign form is the donor's own description. Employers typed differently from the firm's name on permits are missed, so the counts are floors. A connection beside a fast record is a reason to look at the individual permits, not a finding about either.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"firm","t":"Firm or licensed professional","type":"org"},{"k":"standsOut","t":"Consistently fast on","type":"text"},{"k":"links","t":"Kinds of connection","type":"int"},{"k":"gave","t":"Given to candidates by staff or firm","type":"usd"},{"k":"gaveN","t":"Contributions","type":"int"},{"k":"gaveTo","t":"Committees","type":"int"},{"k":"gaveYears","t":"Years","type":"text"},{"k":"lobby","t":"Lobbyist contacts as client","type":"int"},{"k":"lobbyWhere","t":"Mostly with","type":"text"},{"k":"gifts","t":"Gifts to officials or departments","type":"int"},{"k":"registered","t":"Registered permit consultant","type":"text"},{"k":"vendor","t":"Paid by the City since fiscal 2019","type":"usd"},{"k":"former","t":"Former City staff (name match)","type":"text"},{"k":"listed","t":"Case file or extra-scrutiny list","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"firm":"Pacific Gas and Electric","firmKey":null,"standsOut":"Public Works street permits","links":5,"gave":24159,"gaveN":104,"gaveTo":61,"gaveYears":"2012–2026","lobby":964,"lobbyWhere":"Mayor; has its own registered lobbyists","gifts":2,"registered":"","vendor":381535150,"former":"","listed":""},{"firm":"A.R. Sanchez-Corea & Associates","firmKey":null,"standsOut":"Building permits (holds, stations, reaching issue)","links":4,"gave":2600,"gaveN":7,"gaveTo":6,"gaveYears":"2012–2022","lobby":null,"lobbyWhere":"has its own registered lobbyists","gifts":1,"registered":"Since 2015-01-05","vendor":null,"former":"","listed":""},{"firm":"SIA Consulting Corp","firmKey":null,"standsOut":"Building permits (holds, stations, reaching issue)","links":3,"gave":12200,"gaveN":35,"gaveTo":16,"gaveYears":"2012–2023","lobby":null,"lobbyWhere":"","gifts":1,"registered":"","vendor":null,"former":"","listed":"Named in the case 